{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And I will send among you</b> etc. Corresponding to 'and I will remove evil beasts' — the measure of goodness exceeds the measure of punishment, for in the blow it is not written 'evil beast.'" "<b>And it shall bereave you.</b> Corresponding to 'and you shall pursue your enemies' — since until now you were pursuing, now you will cease pursuing, for you will be bereaved." "<b>And it shall cut off your cattle.</b> Corresponding to 'from the land' — which is a blessing in its own right. For its meaning is: I will remove the evil beast from among you, and likewise I will eliminate it from the land, which is the dwelling place of cattle." "<b>And I will diminish you.</b> Corresponding to 'and I will multiply you.'" "<b>And your roads shall be desolate.</b> Corresponding to 'and I will give peace in the land.' These are seven punishments, as Rashi explained."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:32.944885270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}